---
import AtlasLayout from '../layouts/AtlasLayout.astro';
---

<AtlasLayout
  title="Methodology"
  description="How the Science-Based Lifting Atlas scopes, reviews, and publishes evidence."
  current="methodology"
>
  <article class="method-page">
    <header class="method-page__header">
      <p class="kicker">Methodology / living document</p>
      <h1>How the atlas earns a statement.</h1>
      <p>
        This project is produced with AI systems under human product ownership.
        AI review is not credentialed expert or peer review. The workflow is
        designed to make that constraint visible and auditable.
      </p>
    </header>

    <aside class="method-page__notice" aria-label="Publication status">
      <strong>No scientific claim is public yet.</strong>
      <span>
        The first evidence slice passed independent AI review but remains
        publication-locked until owner approval and an immutable manifest.
      </span>
    </aside>

    <div class="method-page__grid">
      <section aria-labelledby="roles-title">
        <p class="method-page__number">01</p>
        <h2 id="roles-title">Separated roles</h2>
        <p>
          Claude Research gathers and extracts evidence. Codex implements the
          system and integrates approved records. A distinct Claude account
          audits the candidate without repairing what it reviews.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="claims-title">
        <p class="method-page__number">02</p>
        <h2 id="claims-title">Atomic claims</h2>
        <p>
          Factual prose is stored as structured claims with source locators,
          certainty, applicability, limitations, review dates, and lifecycle
          state. Pages reuse those records rather than rewriting the facts.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="conflict-title">
        <p class="method-page__number">03</p>
        <h2 id="conflict-title">Conflict stays visible</h2>
        <p>
          Supporting, qualifying, and contradictory sources remain linked to the
          claim. Disagreement is resolved from sources or by weakening or
          withholding the claim—not by averaging reviewer confidence.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="publish-title">
        <p class="method-page__number">04</p>
        <h2 id="publish-title">Fail-closed publication</h2>
        <p>
          Public rendering requires an approved record, explicit owner approval,
          an immutable manifest, a matching content checksum, and current source
          status. Missing any one of them blocks the page.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</AtlasLayout>
